From 1be9b5489db23e3d4f500c7255730bb995ce8730 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:29:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 74/76] doc/examples/transcode: pass the color properties on to
 the encoder

The video encoder is set up with the size and the sample aspect ratio
of the decoder, but not with its color properties. The output is
written without color range, primaries, transfer characteristics and
matrix, even though the input has them:

  $ ffprobe -show_entries stream=color_range,color_space,color_transfer,color_primaries in.mp4
  color_range=tv
  color_space=bt709
  color_transfer=bt709
  color_primaries=bt709
  $ doc/examples/transcode in.mp4 out.mp4
  $ ffprobe -show_entries stream=color_range,color_space,color_transfer,color_primaries out.mp4
  color_range=unknown
  color_space=unknown
  color_transfer=unknown
  color_primaries=unknown

A player then has to guess, and typically treats an HD stream as
BT.601 or a limited-range stream as full range, which changes the
colors. Encoders such as libx264 write these values to the stream from
the codec context, so copy them from the decoder context, next to the
aspect ratio, together with the chroma sample location. The properties
already reach the filter graph since the buffer source gets them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FZ4G6798n6Ua4qu6xwWu3S
---
 doc/examples/transcode.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/doc/examples/transcode.c b/doc/examples/transcode.c
index d0ccbf3..7c0f73c 100644
--- a/doc/examples/transcode.c
+++ b/doc/examples/transcode.c
@@ -176,6 +176,11 @@ static int open_output_file(const char *filename)
                 enc_ctx->height = dec_ctx->height;
                 enc_ctx->width = dec_ctx->width;
                 enc_ctx->sample_aspect_ratio = dec_ctx->sample_aspect_ratio;
+                enc_ctx->color_range = dec_ctx->color_range;
+                enc_ctx->color_primaries = dec_ctx->color_primaries;
+                enc_ctx->color_trc = dec_ctx->color_trc;
+                enc_ctx->colorspace = dec_ctx->colorspace;
+                enc_ctx->chroma_sample_location = dec_ctx->chroma_sample_location;
 
                 ret = avcodec_get_supported_config(enc_ctx, NULL,
                                                    AV_CODEC_CONFIG_PIX_FORMAT, 0,
